Upgrading from IBM Software Hub Version 5.1 to Version 5.3
Last Updated: 2026-07-15

A Red Hat® OpenShift® Container Platform cluster administrator and instance administrator can work together to upgrade IBM Software Hub from Version 5.1 to Version 5.3.
Important: All of the services that are associated with an instance of IBM Software Hub must be upgraded to the same version. For example:

    If you want to upgrade an instance of IBM Software Hub to Version 5.3.1, you must upgrade all of the services that are installed on the instance to Version 5.3.1.
    If you want to upgrade a service to Version 5.3.1, you must upgrade the instance of IBM Software Hub where the service is installed and upgrade all of the services that are installed on the instance to Version 5.3.1.

Before you begin
Before you upgrade IBM Software Hub:

    Review the information in the Planning section.

    Specifically, ensure that you review the System requirements. Your cluster must have sufficient resources.
    Review the information in Planning an upgrade.
    Ensure that you have a copy of script that defines the installation environment variables for your deployment.

    The script enables you to run most of the installation and upgrade commands without modifying them.
    If you are currently using the IBM Certificate manager, migrate to the Red Hat OpenShift Certificate manager (cert-manager Operator). For details, see Migrating from the IBM Certificate manager to the Red Hat OpenShift Certificate manager.
    Best practice Backup your IBM Software Hub installation before you upgrade.

    In the event of an unrecoverable failure, you can use the backup to recover your existing installation. For details, see Backing up and restoring IBM Software Hub in the IBM Software Hub Version 5.1 documentation.

Services that cannot be upgraded from Version 5.1 to Version 5.3

IBM StreamSets
    You cannot upgrade IBM StreamSets from IBM Software Hub Version 5.1.0, 5.1.1, or 5.1.2 to Version 5.3.
    You must remove the IBM StreamSets components and re-install the service on Version 5.3. 

